 .../root/usr/libexec/pejir-awg-watch          | 134 ++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 164 insertions(+)
 create mode 100755 package/pejir-awg/root/etc/init.d/50-pejir-awg-watch
 create mode 100755 package/pejir-awg/root/usr/libexec/pejir-awg-watch

diff --git a/package/pejir-awg/Makefile b/package/pejir-awg/Makefile
index 3ecdfe15..4c707441 100644
--- a/package/pejir-awg/Makefile
+++ b/package/pejir-awg/Makefile
@@ -31,6 +31,13 @@ define Package/pejir-awg/description
   libchacha20poly1305, libcurve25519, amneziawg) and then re-runs "ifup"
   for every amneziawg/wireguard interface, so the tunnel starts right
   after boot and after the network configuration is reloaded.
+
+  It also ships a watchdog for the tunnel. When all router traffic is
+  routed through AmneziaWG, a stuck tunnel takes the whole internet down
+  with it: the default route points into the tunnel and nothing gets
+  through. The watchdog restarts a silent tunnel and, if it does not
+  come back, removes the default route so the router falls back to LTE
+  on its own.
 endef
 
